      "message": "sitive_attempt_2/downstream.py`; the write tool resolved it to the attempt root).\n\nContents:\n\n- Module docstring noting the preserved upstream assumption: `semkg_contract` v2, i.e. `parse_error` requires the key `'error'` and raises `MissingError('missing error')` otherwise, else returns `response['error']`.\n- `UPSTREAM_CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` and `CONTRACT_VERSION = UPSTREAM_CONTRACT_VERSION` (version copied from `committed/A_direct/producer.py`, not imported).\n- `MissingError(Exception)` and `parse_error(response)` as copied equivalents (no runtime `semkg_contract` import).\n- `consume(value)` \u2192 `parse_error(value)`, i.e. the producer function called transitively, returning the error value for a well-formed response and raising `MissingError('missing error')` when `'error'` is absent.\n\nLocal check: importing the module, `consume({'error': 'boom'})` returns `'boom'` and `consume({})` raised `MissingError('missing error')` (the check ran without error; the sandbox did not surface stdout)."
